{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Chains of gold.</b> Chains." "<b>At the edge.</b> At the end of the border of the choshen you shall make them." "<b>Work of braiding.</b> Work of braiding threads — and not work of holes and loops like those made for buckets, but like those made for halters, which are called אנשנשוי\"רש בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>And you shall set the chains.</b> Of the braided cords made in the work of braiding — upon these settings. And this is not the place of the command for their making of the chains, nor the command for their setting: the תַּעֲשֶׂה spoken of here is not the language of command, and the וְנָתַתָּה spoken of here is not the language of command, but the language of the future — for in the parashah of the choshen He returns and commands about their making and their setting, and it was written here only to inform of part of the need of the settings that He commanded to make with the ephod. And He wrote you this to tell you: these settings you will need — when you make chains at the edges of the choshen, you will set them upon these settings."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French eneisnoier or chanfrein-related, denoting an animal's halter/headstall"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:12.567168299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}